it's been 16 years since the first  psychonauts  game but on august 25th we're finally  getting a sequel to the cult classic  that's a lot to live up to  and thankfully from five hours of  hands-on time with the preview version  of the game  i can tell you this that it is  bolstering  with double fine's signature creativity  while also  tackling some pretty serious topics of  mental health  with more intentionality than the first  one ever did  the result is as ambitious as it is  inspiring  so let's get into it the story picks up  only hours after the first game in  moments after the vr sequel interlude  psychonauts and the rhombus of ruin  10 year old psychic prodigy rest spun  has saved the leader of the psychonauts  truman  zenato with the help of fellow  psychonaut agents from the grips  of the maniacal dentist amateur brain  surgeon  dr lobato let's check out those  choppers the first level kicks off with  you entering the mind of dr lobato to  find out who hired him to kidnap truman  all you need to do is get this vacation  request  approved by your supervisor what  once lovato becomes aware there's agents  inside of his head his dental background  starts to protrude through the office  walls  quite literally and it's eerie as it is  inspiring that's gross the level  equally acts as a tutorial teaching  players how to maneuver with double  jumps wall jumping as well as briefing  on returning abilities that players from  the original will  be pretty familiar with however with a  lot of quality of life improvements that  make them a whole lot  better telekinesis for example now  operates more like the game control so  items nearby will automatically come to  you  making it easy to launch it at an enemy  pyrokinesis forms an area of attack  bubble to better visualize its execution  and cyblast has a cooldown rather than  having to collect  aggression ammo all of these  improvements actually made this one feel  more actiony than the first one which is  a good thing because  in this case it felt tight it feels  refined especially  with the addition of a dodge button  through lobato's mine i encountered  mainstay enemies from the first game  like the sensors  but also an array of new enemies like  regrets flying creatures that carry  heavy weights to drop on you  now one of the most effective ways to  kill these buggers because they're  flying  is by using the long range ability  cyblast  the moment i did that i was able to pick  up one of its weights and launch it  right into a sensor  and it was very very satisfying  with the introduction of each new enemy  i was conditioned to change my playing  style often switching out abilities to  control the onslaught  new enemies like doubt sludge-like  creatures that can slow you down  are highly flammable so pyrokinesis came  in clutch while enablers support enemies  that make foes invincible  were fast and agile requiring the use of  time bubble  a new ability that temporarily slows an  enemy in place giving me the chance to  lay in on the beatdown  the constant introduction of different  enemy types learning their weaknesses  and understanding the abilities on hand  offered consistent variety with multiple  methods to tackle the situation  most impressive is double fine's  interlacing of conceptual design with  its enemies like using feelings of  regret  doubt and enabling as literal  interpretations for enemy types  but like the first game it's not all  about the action but moments of  exploration  too in psychonauts 2 the psychonauts  headquarters known as the motherlobe  is akin to the whispering rock sidekick  summer camp from the first game  a wide and open connective hub-like area  upon entering the hq you're greeted with  a towering mural of the organization's  leaders known as the psychic six  the room is alive with agents talking to  each other bustling around  reading books or having lunch you can  hear the thoughts of some agents while  others use their abilities to tend to  watering plants or  levitate to other platforms hi i'm sorry  i just hate children a brain in a  hamster ball is rolling around  sorry there's a rat and a leather jacket  and voices reverberate from the pa  system this area is also the  introduction to many new  characters of psychonauts 2 including  hollis forsythe the no-nonsense  second head of psychonauts and now rez's  new teacher  and because this is psychonauts when raz  goes to class he actually enters the  minds of his  teachers and it's during this moment  when you enter hollis mind  that the game starts to show the depth  of his characterization  when raz is in there he learns the  ability mental connection which can be  used to interconnect a person's thoughts  or  even completely change their mind when  raz uses mental connection to  accidentally change forsythe's mind to  associate risk with delight  her mental state begins to unravel as  elements of her past as a doctor start  to transfuse with gambling oh  no looks like hollis had a spontaneous  change in her world view  themes of guilt fear and risk are  intertwined with old-style vegas and  hospitals  resulting in raz having to gamble with  literal concepts of life and death as a  puzzle element  to proceed and in the process learns  more about forsythe's character beyond  her stern and hard exterior  but the most shining example of level  design themes and gameplay  all working symbiotically is copton's  cook-off which is  absolutely hilarious and kind of  disturbing  it's time for  the whole thing is a take on performance  anxiety it's intense race against the  clock to gather animated talking  ingredients like eggs fruits and meats  to boil in water  blend in a blender or get sliced by a  giant hatchet  all the while using the environment to  grind between cooking stations and avoid  obstacles like  giant cheese grinders or hot plates all  of which was  peppered with comical tongue-in-cheek  commercial breaks but in the end it's a  heartfelt and considerate take on a  character  struggling with eternal judgment and  unworthiness amongst his peers  you can do it next one won't be so easy  but in a continuous clashing of concepts  and design  the next level was a complete 180 from  the anxiety-induced cook-off nightmare  instead of the concentrated stress fest  of the last level this one was  wide in scope and ambitious in its  display of a fantasy reflective of the  character's mind that it takes place in  cassie is a teacher who loves big worlds  storytelling  and literature and therefore the level  itself is  big adventurous and made up of literal  books  for cassie her personal problems is that  she's had trouble letting go  and for a coping mechanism in her mind  she's created multiple versions of  herself that are  literally buried in the books she loves  cassie you gotta watch out  there's a giant uh you  out there hunting for you in order to  help  face cassie's biggest foe herself i had  to navigate a fantastical world made up  of  paper castles sail on paper made boats  hop through  literal pages and use written sentences  as my platforms  to find the other versions of herself on  the surface psychonauts 2 is shaping up  to be an engaging ambitious honed  in take on colorful three platformers  however  the most promising aspect hasn't just  been returning to its world mastering  its platforms or combat  but peeling back the layers to see  what's beneath it to take a closer look  at its characters  the depth of their struggles fears and  regrets  all of which serve as the foundation and  inspiration for the world's you traverse  and all that has left me very very eager  to see what it means for the sequel when  it launches on august 25th  if you're a fan of psychonauts consider  checking out a retrospective i did on  the first one  you can find a link to that in the  description below additionally i did a  written  version of this preview as well which  you can find on our website at  gamespot.com  which has a little bit more detail as  well as some tidbits from an interview i  did with the game's director  tim schaefer and art director lissette  teatri montgomery so again  links below all right thanks for  watching hope this was helpful to you  till next time see you later  [Music]  you
 

